  "title": "Segments Left",
  "briefing": "The same underlay still prefers RTR-1 -> RTR-3 -> RTR-5, but SRv6 steers an IPv4 payload with an IPv6 Segment Routing Header instead of MPLS labels. Open RTR-1's V6 tab and add Policy-1. Set Dest to 10.0.35.2 and enter these comma-separated SIDs in policy order: 2001:db8:2::1, 2001:db8:4::1, 2001:db8:5::1. The SRH is encoded in reverse on the wire, while the active IPv6 destination advances through this human-readable order and Segments Left counts down. Send a packet from RTR-1 to RTR-5 when the policy is ACTIVE.",
